              {spokes.map((s) => (
                <li><a href={s.href}><span class="bp-n">{s.n}</span><span class="bp-l">{s.label}</span><span class="bp-t">{s.tag}</span></a></li>
              ))}
            </ol>
          </nav>

          <h3>By Subspecies: Congo, Timneh, Baby, Pairs</h3>
          <p>Start with <a href="/congo-african-grey-for-sale/">the Congo page</a> or <a href="/timneh-african-grey-for-sale/">the Timneh page</a> if the fork above settled it for you. <a href="/baby-african-grey-parrot-for-sale/">The baby page</a> is for buyers who want a chick still finishing weaning, and there are two pair pages: <a href="/congo-african-grey-parrot-pair-for-sale/">the companion pair</a> for a household, and <a href="/african-grey-breeding-pair-for-sale/">breeding pairs</a> for aviculturists.</p>

          <h3>By Guarantee: Health, DNA, Hand-Raised, Documentation</h3>
          <p>If what you want is the proof, the spokes are <a href="/african-greys-for-sale-with-health-guarantee/">the health guarantee page</a>, <a href="/dna-tested-african-grey-for-sale/">DNA-tested greys</a>, <a href="/hand-raised-african-grey-parrot-for-sale/">what hand-raised means here</a> and <a href="/cites-african-grey-documentation/">the documentation page</a>.</p>

          <h3>By Place: Your State or Metro</h3>
          <p>Geography has one page, and this is not it.</p>
          <h4>One Link to the Near-Me Router, Not a Grid</h4>
          <p><a href="/african-grey-parrots-for-sale-near-me/">The near-you page</a> lists every state and metro we have written a page for and routes you to yours. We ship to all fifty states whether or not yours has a page.</p>
          <h5>Why the Hub Enumerates No States</h5>
          <p>Because two pages listing the same forty destinations would compete with each other in search and confuse a buyer about which one to trust. The router owns the list; the hub owns the birds.</p>
          <h6>Across the Cluster: Eggs, Adoption Cost and Buying With Shipping</h6>
          <p>Three spokes sit outside the usual questions: <a href="/african-grey-parrot-bird-eggs-for-sale-usa/">fertile eggs</a>, <a href="/african-grey-parrot-adoption-cost/">adoption and first-year cost</a>, and <a href="/buy-african-grey-parrots-with-shipping/">buying with shipping</a>, which is the page for a buyer who has already decided and wants the price proved.</p>
        </section>

        <div class="seam-wrap"><img class="seam" src={seam} alt="" loading="lazy" width="182" height="60" decoding="async"></div>

        <!-- ===================== §8 · FAQ-C, REFRESHED WITH SPOKE LINKS ===================== -->
