          <h3>Price and Deposits</h3>
          <p>Questions one, two, three and eight above. The short version: the card price is the price, the deposit is {deposit}, and a grey under $1,000 is a listing to walk away from.</p>
          <h3>Legality, CITES and Paperwork</h3>
          <p>Questions five and six. Owning a grey hatched in captivity is lawful; the six documents are what make it provable.</p>
          <h3>Pairs, Babies and Adoption</h3>
          <p>Questions two, nine and ten. A companion pair is two unrelated birds sold together, a baby is a chick that leaves once weaned, and adoption is a good route when a rescue near you has the right bird.</p>
